# Checking identities and answers

Put ≟ (typed as `?=`) between two sides to check them. Math++ tries a
symbolic proof first, then compares the sides at random points, and marks the line ✓ or ✗;
a ✗ shows a point where the sides differ.

## Identities

$$ \sin^2 x + \cos^2 x \overset{?}{=} 1 $$

$$ \sin 2x \overset{?}{=} 2 \sin x \cos x $$

$$ \cos 2x \overset{?}{=} \cos^2 x - \sin^2 x $$

$$ \tan^2 x + 1 \overset{?}{=} \sec^2 x $$

$$ \sin(x + y) \overset{?}{=} \sin x \cos y + \cos x \sin y $$

$$ \cosh^2 x - \sinh^2 x ≟ 1 $$

$$ (a + b)^2 ?= a^2 + 2ab + b^2 $$

## Homework answers

$$ \frac{d}{dx} x^2 \sin x \overset{?}{=} 2x \sin x + x^2 \cos x $$

$$ \int x e^x \, dx \overset{?}{=} (x - 1) e^x $$

An antiderivative may differ from Math++'s by a constant and still be right:

$$ \int \sin x \cos x \, dx \overset{?}{=} -\frac{\cos^2 x}{2} $$

$$ \lim_{x \to 0} \frac{1 - \cos x}{x^2} \overset{?}{=} \frac{1}{2} $$

$$ \sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{1}{2^n} \overset{?}{=} 1 $$

## Mistakes

$$ (x + 1)^2 \overset{?}{=} x^2 + 1 $$

$$ \sqrt{x^2} \overset{?}{=} x $$

$$ \frac{d}{dx} \ln(2x) \overset{?}{=} \frac{2}{x} $$

$$ \int_0^1 x^2 \, dx \overset{?}{=} \frac{1}{2} $$
